      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1978, Corktown’s residential core earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places, cementing its architectural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corktown%2C_Detroit",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ford’s 2017 purchase of The Factory building sparked a new urban campus, later expanding to Michigan Central Station and Roosevelt Warehouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corktown%2C_Detroit",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Latino workers from the Southwest and Mexico began settling in Corktown in the 1920s, adding a vibrant cultural layer to the area.",
